course: dictionary
lesson: 6684
title: Observer: a person who watches
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An observer is a person who watches something carefully. Some observers watch to learn, and some watch so they can report what happened. Context helps you check this. «In science lessons a good observer looks closely and writes down what they see.» The words looks closely and writes down tell you the observer is paying close attention.
explain: «In the UK and Ireland paper votes are counted by hand in front of observers from every party.» Here the observers do not count the votes. They stand and watch, so the count is fair. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Words can also show how much attention someone pays. «She is a keen observer» means she notices things eagerly. «A casual observer» watches without paying much attention. Keen and casual are both clues, so read the words next to observer carefully.
fact: An observer is a person who watches something carefully.
fact: In science, observation is the first step of an experiment, so a good observer looks closely and writes down what they see.
fact: At an election, observers watch the votes being counted to check that it is fair.
fact: «A keen observer» means someone who notices things eagerly, while «a casual observer» means someone who watches without paying close attention.
exercise: «In science lessons a good observer looks closely and writes down what they see.» What is a good observer? | Someone who only talks during science | *Someone who looks closely and writes down what they see | Someone who never writes anything down | Someone who closes their eyes to think
exercise: «Observers from every party watch the votes being counted.» What is an observer's job there? | To vote twice in the same election | *To watch and check that the count is fair | To count the votes with their own pen | To make the rules of the election
exercise: In the phrase «a casual observer», what does casual suggest? | Very careful and serious | Hungry and tired | Very loud and noisy | *Relaxed, without paying close attention
test: «A good observer notices small things that others miss.» What does a good observer do? | Forgets everything very quickly | *Notices small things that others miss | Talks loudly over everyone else | Hides from the things happening around them
test: «There is no bright south pole star, so southern observers find south using the long arm of the Southern Cross.» How do southern observers find south? | By asking a passing ship for directions | By counting the penguins on the shore | By following a bright south pole star | *By using the long arm of the Southern Cross
exam: Which sentence shows an observer who watches an event but does not take part? | The team's observer scored the winning goal. | Our observer cooked dinner for everyone. | *Observers from every party watched the votes being counted. | The observer painted the kitchen door blue.
